  ["To every thing there is a season", ["\"To every thing there is a season, and a time to every purpose under the heaven\" (Ecclesiastes 3:1). Joseph stored grain in the years of plenty so his family could stand in the years of famine (Genesis 41). Wise women prepare in the bull and stay faithful in the bear."]],
  ["What to do in each season", ["In a bull market: keep investing steadily, rebalance if stocks have grown beyond your target, build your emergency fund, and resist get-rich-quick temptations.",
    "In a bear market: keep investing if you can, avoid selling in panic, rebalance if your mix has drifted, and remember that lower prices mean your regular investment buys more shares."]],
